 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "In 1973, a truck hit the only tree for 250 miles.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 4.699
  },
  {
   "text": "The Tree of T\u00e9n\u00e9r\u00e9 stood alone in the Sahara.",
   "s": 4.998,
   "e": 6.985
  },
  {
   "text": "Its roots reached more than 100 feet down to find water.",
   "s": 7.285,
   "e": 10.379
  },
  {
   "text": "So caravans steered by it, and maps marked it like a city.",
   "s": 10.679,
   "e": 13.601
  },
  {
   "text": "Thousands of camels passed it, but none knocked it down.",
   "s": 13.902,
   "e": 16.409
  },
  {
   "text": "Then a truck came down the old caravan trail.",
   "s": 16.709,
   "e": 18.658
  },
  {
   "text": "So how do you hit the only tree in the desert?",
   "s": 18.958,
   "e": 20.959
  },
  {
   "text": "Rumor says the driver was drunk. The trunk snapped.",
   "s": 21.379,
   "e": 23.759
  },
  {
   "text": "Today its dead trunk sits in a museum.",
   "s": 24.059,
   "e": 25.789
  },
  {
   "text": "Its replacement is metal. Let's see a truck try.",
   "s": 26.089,
   "e": 28.435
  }
 ],
